<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">//Ad secundum, quod aequalitas illa est</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">arithmetica habet latitudinē ex parte</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">valoris mercium, cum quo coaequandū</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">est pretium. //Ad tertium, quod indiui¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">sibilitas numeri rerum, quę in argumē¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">to sumuntur attenditur per coęquatio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">nem intellectus ad rem, quę indiuisibi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">lis est, &amp; non pendet ex nostra opinio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">ne, &amp; affectu: sed aequalitas pretij iusti,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">non sumitur ex re ipsa, sed ex aestima¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">tione, &amp; affectu plurium hominum, &amp;</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">communitatis, quae magnam includunt</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">latitudinem.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">##SECVNDVM DVBIVM</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">#Quae nò sint attendenda in re¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">#cta aestimatione pretij.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">##SVMMARIVM.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">>>>31 Quidam pro regula ponunt, rem</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">>>tantum valere, quanti vendi po¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_20">>>test.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">>>>32 Reprobatur haec regula, &amp; contra¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">>>ria statuitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">>>>33 Probatur ratione non esse veram</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">>>regulam.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">>>>34 Subuertit haec fallax regula omnem</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">>>doctrinam huius contractus de</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">>>emptione pretio iusto.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">>>>35 An saltem sit vera regula in emptio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">>>ne, quae fit pretio conuentionali</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">>>>36 Quidam id affirmant, sed malè.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">>>>37 Effroenata licentia ascendendi enor¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">>>miter in pretio rerum venalium</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">>>exquisitarum ratione cohibenda</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">>>est, &amp; iudicio prudentum.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">>>>38 Probatur ratione non licere etiam</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">>>tum immodicè in pretio magis, ac</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">>>magis ascendere.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">>>>39 Ad argumenta in contrarium re¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">>>spondetur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">>>>40 Prima regula est, non esse iustum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">>>pretium quanti vendi res potest</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">>>maximi.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">>>>41 Secunda regula est, non esse attenden¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">>>dam perfectionem rei venditae in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">>>esse naturae.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">>>>42 Fallax etiam tertia regula est necessi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">>>tas, aut vtilitas emptoris.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">>>>43 Quarta regula, non esse aestimandum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">>>pretium secundum expensas, la¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">>>borem, aut industriam, aut pe¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">>>riculum venditoris.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_55">>>>44 Non qui magis laborauit, aut magis</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">>>expendit, aut maiorem industriā</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_57">>>apposuit, aut maius periculum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_58">>>subijt, maius meretur pretium.</line>
</lines>
